.TH ZIONSTATSD 1 "2026-10-19" "zionstats 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zionstatsd \- always-on GPU telemetry daemon publishing shared-memory frames
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zionstatsd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Polls GPU telemetry, publishes 256 KiB frames to
.IR /dev/shm/zionstats-<uid>
(mode 0600, seqlock + flock single-writer), serves
.B /metrics
(Prometheus/OpenMetrics), /snapshot, and /healthz on the metrics socket,
and drives the fail-safe cooling controller.  SIGHUP reloads the config:
fans restore to driver control, plugs are left as-is, and the actuation
belief re-syncs within one readback period.  SIGTERM applies the
configured plug shutdown policy and restores fan control.
.SH OPTIONS
Same options as
.BR zionstats (1):
.BR \-i / \-\-interval ,
.B \-\-host ,
.B \-\-port ,
.B \-\-readonly ,
.B \-\-demo ,
.BI \-\-provider ,
.BI \-\-record ,
.BI \-\-replay ,
.BI \-\-config ,
.BI \-\-mode ,
.B \-\-check\-config .
.SH METRICS
Default bind 127.0.0.1:9400.  Bearer auth via the [export] token config
key (config only, never CLI).  dcgm-exporter also defaults to :9400 --
set [daemon] port for mixed stacks.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zionstats (1),
.BR zionstats-tui (1)
